---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHead from "../../components/PageHead.astro";
import State from "../../components/State.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../site";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Roadmap"
  description="The Zacess roadmap: the website and code themes done, an early browser version now, then apps for every platform. Five phases from v0 to v4, each with an honest status."
>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="Roadmap"
    title="Where Zacess is going"
    lead="The core that does the real work is built and tested. Next is putting it in people's hands, one useful step at a time."
  />

  <section aria-labelledby="order-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="order-title">What comes next</h2>
      <p class="intro">The apps are not ready to install yet. This is the order things arrive in.</p>
      <ol class="roadmap">
        <li>
          <p class="when">Done</p>
          <h3>This website and the code themes</h3>
          <p>What Zacess is, how it works, how to follow along and our accessibility statement, plus the eight contrast themes as <a href="/themes/">code themes</a> for editors and terminals.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="current">
          <p class="when">Now</p>
          <h3>The browser version</h3>
          <p>Open a file in your browser, read it in your profile, listen to it and export it, with no account to make. An early version is <a href="https://app.zacess.com">open to try now</a>.</p>
          <p><a href="#browser-title">What the browser version will include</a></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="when">Later</p>
          <h3>The apps</h3>
          <p>Windows, macOS, Linux, iOS and Android, built on the same core, with lecture capture on your phone, the share sheet, a desktop shortcut and a browser extension.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="browser-title">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2 id="browser-title">What the browser version will include</h2>
      <p>The browser version is the next release. The core runs in your browser as WebAssembly, with pdf.js for PDFs and tesseract.js for text recognition. It will include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Open your material:</strong> PDFs, images with text recognition, Word files and web pages.</li>
        <li><strong>Reading profiles:</strong> the presets, your own profiles and the contrast themes.</li>
        <li><strong>Read aloud:</strong> whole documents with the voices built into your browser and device.</li>
        <li><strong>Magnifier and zoom:</strong> through your reading profile and your browser's own zoom.</li>
        <li><strong>Export:</strong> accessible HTML, EPUB 3 and braille-ready files.</li>
        <li><strong>No account:</strong> see <a href="/privacy/">how Zacess handles your files</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You will be able to install it like an app. The <a href="/features/">features page</a> marks everything that comes with it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="phases-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="phases-title">The five phases</h2>
      <p class="intro">Each phase is useful on its own: v0 can help real students without lecture recording, sync or AI. Every phase is tested with people who have different access needs before it ships.</p>
      <ol class="roadmap wide">
        <li>
          <p class="when">v0</p>
          <h3>Make documents readable</h3>
          <State status="built" note="most of v0, with the rest in the browser version or later" />
          <ul>
            <li>Import PDFs and images, with OCR where there is no text layer. Built in the core.</li>
            <li>Confidence marking, correction and comparison with the original. Marking and correction are built; side-by-side comparison comes later.</li>
            <li>Reading profiles with presets and light and dark high-contrast themes. Built in the core.</li>
            <li>A reliable local library with autosave, version history, storage use, backup and restore. Built in the core.</li>
            <li>Accessible HTML and EPUB 3 exports. Built in the core.</li>
            <li>Word import, magnification basics and read aloud. Coming with the browser version.</li>
            <li>PowerPoint import, the full set of personal audio controls and DOCX and MP3 exports. Later.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="when">v1</p>
          <h3>Make lectures accessible</h3>
          <State status="built" note="the camera, microphone and screens come later with the apps" />
          <ul>
            <li>Slide capture from the projector that skips repeats.</li>
            <li>Audio recording that survives a crash or a flat battery.</li>
            <li>Transcription and live captions.</li>
            <li>Searchable transcripts, bookmarks, chapter markers and one timeline where you can jump to any sentence or slide.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="when">v2</p>
          <h3>Make learning easier</h3>
          <State status="built" note="much of v2, with the rest later" />
          <ul>
            <li>Built in the core: FSRS flashcards, reading goals with no streak pressure, revision paths, Anki and Notion export, whiteboard capture with every version kept, maths and engineering mode, universal capture, bilingual reading and braille-ready output.</li>
            <li>Later: joined handwriting, advanced equation recognition, the browser extension, right-to-left layout in the reading view and more interface languages.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="when">v3</p>
          <h3>Connect students and institutions</h3>
          <State status="later" note="the sync rules are already built in the core" />
          <ul>
            <li>Sync across your devices, with an optional account to sync your library across the apps and the website. Zacess works fully without one and an account is never required.</li>
            <li>Accessible collaboration with permission controls, keeping your own profile separate from the shared source.</li>
            <li>Lecturer mode: a live slide feed that every student receives in their own profile.</li>
            <li>Connections to Blackboard, Moodle, Canvas, OneDrive and Google Drive, one at a time.</li>
            <li>University deployment and the optional paid tier.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="when">v4</p>
          <h3>Add optional intelligence</h3>
          <State status="later" />
          <ul>
            <li>Diagram descriptions, "explain simply", answers about your own lectures with their sources, outlines, quizzes and flashcards, OCR clean-up and glossaries.</li>
            <li>Models on your device first, the cloud only for heavy jobs in the paid tier, always optional and labelled. See <a href="/privacy/#ai-title">the AI rules</a>.</li>
            <li>The groundwork is in the core already: searching your own material with sources plus two helpers that use no AI model.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="follow-title">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2 id="follow-title">Follow along</h2>
      <p>News and releases are posted in <a href={SITE.discussions}>Zacess Discussions on GitHub</a>. Ideas for the roadmap are welcome there too.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
